@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product] monospace-component-boundary
Components MUST emit semantic HTML styled by the Monospace Web stylesheet:
sizes in character cells and line heights, colours only through the four
presentation tokens, state conveyed by text, weight or inverse video, and icons
as text glyphs. Components MUST NOT reference external resources or utility
class frameworks. Element ids, data attributes, ARIA names and hook names that
tests and browser probes consume MUST stay stable across presentation changes;
presentation code MUST NOT acquire domain mutation authority.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] component-untrusted-content
Components MUST render user and guest text through HEEx escaping. A caller
MUST NOT pass untrusted strings to raw HTML or executable JavaScript slots.
Terminal bytes belong only in the terminal renderer, never a component's HTML.
